An artwork's Materials field lists the vocabulary's terms to pick from. Only vocabulary editors can add a term; anyone else who tries is told why.

== How this is built ==

* [[Schema:Material]] defines the terms. Its "Subjects are controlled" setting makes them a controlled vocabulary.
* [[Schema:Artwork]] links an artwork to its terms through the Materials relation, while its Medium field keeps the free-text description.
* [[Mapping:EDM]] exports each term as a <code>skos:Concept</code> with <code>skos:exactMatch</code> to its AAT concept, and an artwork's materials as <code>dcterms:medium</code>.
* [[Mapping:CIDOC-CRM]] exports each term as an E57 Material and links an artwork to its terms with P45 consists of.
* [[Special:Subject/s1matvocabaaaaA|Gold leaf on Special:Subject]] lists The Kiss under Referenced by.
* Administrators hold the right to edit Controlled Subjects; [[Special:ListGroupRights]] shows which groups have it.
